## Model card

- **Name:** GPT-6.2 Astra (unreleased — sightings only)
- **Short description:** OpenAI's rumored next flagship after GPT-6 Astra (2026-09-03) / GPT-6.1 Sol. As of 2026-11-13 it has never shipped: the model does not appear in OpenAI's API changelog (checked through 2026-11-05 entries), model docs, or pricing pages; the only traces are an X post about "GPT-6.2 Astra and Sol" appearing on the Google Cloud Console Quotas page (2026-11-04) and a The Information report (paywalled) that GPT-6.2 "could come as soon as Friday" in Astra, Sol and Cyber versions.
- **Provider / access:** none — not announced, not callable, no API route. Sightings: Google Cloud Console Quotas page (2026-11-04, user report); Codex usage breakdowns mentioning `gpt-6.2-astra` (Nov 1–2, per TeamoRouter). OpenAI itself has said nothing.
- **Release / knowledge:** not released. GPT-6 Astra released 2026-09-03; GPT-6.1 Sol 2026-09-29; GPT-6.1 Terra 2026-10-26; GPT-6 Cyber 2026-11-05. GPT-6.2 has no date.
- **IDs:** `gpt-6.2-astra` (seen on Google Cloud quotas; unconfirmed; OpenAI has published no ID).
- **Context window:** unpublished (meta.json claims 1.05M / 128K out — unverified, not evidence).
- **Modalities:** unpublished (presumed text/image in, text out, reasoning).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-13):** none published. (GPT-6 Astra: $10/$50 per 1M >272K prompts priced higher; GPT-6.1 Sol: $2/$10.)
- **Architecture:** unpublished.

